-- title:
--   Products of affine opens over an affine base, with generators
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be an affine scheme and let $f : X \to S$ and $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes, all in a fixed universe. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ which is an affine open, and $V$ an open of $Y$ which is an affine open. Write $p =$ `pullback.fst f g` and $q =$ `pullback.snd f g` for the two projections of the fibre product $X \times_S Y$, and put $W = p^{-1}(U) \cap q^{-1}(V)$, an open of $X \times_S Y$. The assertion is twofold: first, $W$ is an affine open of $X \times_S Y$; second, the subring of $\Gamma(X \times_S Y, W)$ generated by the union of the two sets
--   $$\{\,(p^{\sharp}_U s)|_{W} : s \in \Gamma(X, U)\,\} \quad\text{and}\quad \{\,(q^{\sharp}_V t)|_{W} : t \in \Gamma(Y, V)\,\}$$
--   is the whole of $\Gamma(X \times_S Y, W)$; here $p^{\sharp}_U : \Gamma(X,U) \to \Gamma(X \times_S Y, p^{-1}(U))$ and $q^{\sharp}_V : \Gamma(Y,V) \to \Gamma(X \times_S Y, q^{-1}(V))$ are the components of the morphisms of sheaves attached to $p$ and $q$, and the restrictions are along the inclusions $W \le p^{-1}(U)$ and $W \le q^{-1}(V)$.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic form of the statement that $U \times_S V \cong \operatorname{Spec}(A \otimes_R B)$ when $U = \operatorname{Spec} A$, $V = \operatorname{Spec} B$ and $S = \operatorname{Spec} R$, together with the fact that $A \otimes_R B$ is generated as a ring by the images of $A$ and $B$. It combines [`AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_pullback_fst_preimage_inf_snd_preimage`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_pullback_fst_preimage_inf_snd_preimage) with [`AlgebraicGeometry.closure_range_pullback_fst_appTop_union_range_snd_appTop_eq_top`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.closure_range_pullback_fst_appTop_union_range_snd_appTop_eq_top), and is used in the construction of closed immersions by sections, namely by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.ClosedImmersionBySections.pullback_fst_tensor_pullback_snd`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.ClosedImmersionBySections.pullback_fst_tensor_pullback_snd).
